      <element name="description">
         <element name="abstract">
            <element name="none">
               <field name="value">The teaching through inquiry aims to develop skills by providing an environment in which students work from a problem. The objective of the study was to analyze inquiry-based teaching with 6th-grade students in a public school in the interior of Bahia, focusing on the separation of homogeneous and heterogeneous mixtures. The qualitative research used questionnaires, recordings, and drawings for data collection, analyzed according to Bardin. The central activity was an investigative experimental practice. The students formulated hypotheses, observed, critically analyzed, and systematized the results. The data reveal that inquiry-based teaching favored the understanding of separation methods and promoted greater student engagement in class, contributing to the development of skills such as autonomy, critical thinking, and problem-solving ability. Thus, this approach proved effective for Science teaching, making learning more meaningful and participatory.</field>
            </element>
         </element>
      </element>
